  "question": "Find the value of $p$ for which the projection of $\\vec{a} = (p\\hat{i} + 4\\hat{j})$ on $\\vec{b} = (3\\hat{i} + 4\\hat{j})$ equals 5.",
  "answeroption": "B",
  "explanation": "Projection $= \\frac{\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b}}{|\\vec{b}|}$<br /><br />$\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b} = 3p + 16$<br /><br />$|\\vec{b}| = \\sqrt{3^2+4^2} = 5$<br /><br />So $\\frac{3p + 16}{5} = 5 \\implies 3p + 16 = 25 \\implies 3p = 9 \\implies p = 3$.",
